  cal-20261002-055,s1,h(P^1) = 1 ⊕ 1(-1) in Chow motives.
  cal-20261002-055,s2,"Prismatic cohomology places Hodge–Tate, de Rham and crystalline shadows in one object."
  cal-20261002-055,s3,The noncompressible proof gap is Deligne's Lefschetz-pencil and monodromy argument.
  cal-20261002-055,s4,"The fundamental area cocycle on the rotation algebra: closure supplies the trace, oriented area supplies the calculus."
  cal-20261002-055,s5,"A Wilson step eliminates, rescales and reparametrises."
  cal-20261002-055,s6,"The 2026-09-30 notes open with seven entries on indeterminate beams, the force method, three-moment equation and moment distribution."
  cal-20261002-044,s1,"70 files in the site's visuals, templates, static and scripts reference modelContext (WebMCP)."
  cal-20261002-044,s1,"No Chrome origin-trial token appears in the site's templates, static files or scripts."
  cal-20261002-044,s2,WebMCP's public origin trial began in Chrome 149 on 9 June 2026 and runs to Chrome 156.
  cal-20261002-044,s2,Gemini in Chrome support is described as coming soon.
  cal-20261002-044,s3,Site owners register a token to switch WebMCP on for real users without a browser flag.
  cal-20261002-044,s3,Tools require an open tab; there is no headless execution.
  cal-20261002-044,s4,WebMCP is a Draft Community Group Report; keep it as progressive enhancement over semantic HTML.
